</section><section data-mw-section-id="9" id="mwBZo" aria-labelledby="Operations"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Operations">Operations</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=BP&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9" title="Edit section: Operations"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwBZs"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:BP_North_Sea_Headquarters_-_geograph.org.uk_-_937691.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwBZw"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:BP_North_Sea_Headquarters_-_geograph.org.uk_-_937691.jpg" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/BP_North_Sea_Headquarters_-_geograph.org.uk_-_937691.jpg/250px-BP_North_Sea_Headquarters_-_geograph.org.uk_-_937691.jpg" decoding="async" data-file-width="640" data-file-height="426" data-file-type="bitmap" height="166" width="250" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/BP_North_Sea_Headquarters_-_geograph.org.uk_-_937691.jpg/500px-BP_North_Sea_Headquarters_-_geograph.org.uk_-_937691.jpg 2x" class="mw-file-element" id="mwBZ0"/></a><figcaption id="mwBZ4">BP <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/North_Sea" title="North Sea" id="mwBZ8">North Sea</a> Headquarters, built by the Bowmer and Kirkland group at a cost of £50 million</figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwBaA"><span about="#mwt470" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBaE" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"As of","href":"./Template:As_of"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"2018"},"2":{"wt":"12"},"3":{"wt":"31"}},"i":0}}]}'>As of 31</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt470"> </span><span about="#mwt470">December</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt470"> </span><span about="#mwt470">2018</span><sup class="plainlinks noexcerpt noprint asof-tag update" style="display:none;" about="#mwt470"><a rel="mw:ExtLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=BP&amp;action=edit" class="external text" data-mw-original-href="//en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=BP&amp;action=edit"><span typeof="mw:Entity">[</span>update<span typeof="mw:Entity">]</span></a></sup><span typeof="mw:Nowiki" about="#mwt470"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_potentially_dated_statements_from_December_2018" about="#mwt470"/><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:All_articles_containing_potentially_dated_statements" about="#mwt470" id="mwBaI"/>, BP had operations in 78<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwBaM"> </span>countries worldwide<sup about="#mwt471" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-AR18-glance_206-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"AR18-glance"}}'><a href="#cite_note-AR18-glance-206" id="mwBaQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBaU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBaY">[</span>205<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBac">]</span></span></a></sup> with the global headquarters in London, United Kingdom. BP operations are organized into three business segments, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Upstream_(petroleum_industry)" title="Upstream (petroleum industry)" id="mwBag">Upstream</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Downstream_(petroleum_industry)" title="Downstream (petroleum industry)" id="mwBak">Downstream</a>, and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Renewable_energy" title="Renewable energy" id="mwBao">renewables</a>.<sup about="#mwt472" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-AR18-segments_207-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"AR18-segments"}}'><a href="#cite_note-AR18-segments-207" id="mwBas"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBaw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBa0">[</span>206<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBa4">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwBa8">Since 1951, BP has annually published its <i id="mwBbA">Statistical Review of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/World_Energy" title="World Energy" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBbE">World Energy</a></i>, which is considered an energy industry benchmark.<sup about="#mwt473" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-reuters120613_208-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"reuters120613"}}'><a href="#cite_note-reuters120613-208" id="mwBbI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBbM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBbQ">[</span>207<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBbU">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<section data-mw-section-id="10" id="mwBbY" aria-labelledby="Operations_by_location"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Operations_by_location">Operations by location</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=BP&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10" title="Edit section: Operations by location"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>

<section data-mw-section-id="11" id="mwBbc" aria-labelledby="United_Kingdom"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="United_Kingdom">United Kingdom</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=BP&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11" title="Edit section: United Kingdom"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>

<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwBbg"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Hedon_Clough_and_the_BP_Chemicals_site_at_Saltend_-_geograph.org.uk_-_145508.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwBbk"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Hedon_Clough_and_the_BP_Chemicals_site_at_Saltend_-_geograph.org.uk_-_145508.jpg" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/Hedon_Clough_and_the_BP_Chemicals_site_at_Saltend_-_geograph.org.uk_-_145508.jpg/250px-Hedon_Clough_and_the_BP_Chemicals_site_at_Saltend_-_geograph.org.uk_-_145508.jpg" decoding="async" data-file-width="640" data-file-height="472" data-file-type="bitmap" height="184" width="250" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/Hedon_Clough_and_the_BP_Chemicals_site_at_Saltend_-_geograph.org.uk_-_145508.jpg/500px-Hedon_Clough_and_the_BP_Chemicals_site_at_Saltend_-_geograph.org.uk_-_145508.jpg 2x" class="mw-file-element" id="mwBbo"/></a><figcaption id="mwBbs">The BP chemicals plant in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Salt_End" title="Salt End" id="mwBbw">Saltend</a> near <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingston_upon_Hull" title="Kingston upon Hull" id="mwBb0">Hull</a>, England</figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwBb4">BP has a major corporate campus in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sunbury-on-Thames" title="Sunbury-on-Thames" id="mwBb8">Sunbury-on-Thames</a> which is home to around 3,500<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwBcA"> </span>employees and over 50<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwBcE"> </span>business units.<sup about="#mwt476" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-BP-Sunbury_209-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"BP-Sunbury"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-BP-Sunbury-209"}}'><a href="#cite_note-BP-Sunbury-209" id="mwBcI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBcM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBcQ">[</span>208<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBcU">]</span></span></a></sup> Its <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/North_Sea" title="North Sea" id="mwBcY">North Sea</a> operations are headquartered in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aberdeen" title="Aberdeen" id="mwBcc">Aberdeen</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scotland" title="Scotland" id="mwBcg">Scotland</a>. BP's trading functions are based at <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/20_Canada_Square" title="20 Canada Square" id="mwBck">20 Canada Square</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canary_Wharf" title="Canary Wharf" id="mwBco">Canary Wharf</a>, London. BP has three major research and development centres in the UK.<sup about="#mwt477" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-commons2012_210-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"commons2012"}}'><a href="#cite_note-commons2012-210" id="mwBcs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBcw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBc0">[</span>209<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBc4">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwBc8">As of 2020, and following the sale of its Andrew and Shearwater interests, BP's operations were focussed in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clair_oilfield" title="Clair oilfield" id="mwBdA">Clair</a>, Quad 204 and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eastern_Trough_Area_Project" title="Eastern Trough Area Project" id="mwBdE">ETAP</a> hubs.<sup about="#mwt480" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-211" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-211"}}'><a href="#cite_note-211" id="mwBdI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBdM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBdQ">[</span>210<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBdU">]</span></span></a></sup> In 2011, the company announced that it is focusing its investment in the UK North Sea into four development projects including the Clair, Devenick, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Schiehallion_oilfield" title="Schiehallion oilfield" id="mwBdY">Schiehallion and Loyal</a>, and Kinnoull oilfields.<sup about="#mwt484" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Swint2011_212-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Swint2011"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Swint2011-212"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Swint2011-212" id="mwBdc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBdg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBdk">[</span>211<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBdo">]</span></span></a></sup> BP is the operator of the Clair oilfield, which has been appraised as the largest hydrocarbon resource in the UK.<sup about="#mwt487" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Bawden2011_213-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Bawden2011"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Bawden2011-213"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Bawden2011-213" id="mwBds"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBdw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBd0">[</span>212<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBd4">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwBd8">There are 1,200 BP service stations in the UK.<sup about="#mwt488" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Gosden16_214-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Gosden16"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Gosden16-214" id="mwBeA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBeE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBeI">[</span>213<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBeM">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt489" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-BP-UK_215-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"BP-UK"}}'><a href="#cite_note-BP-UK-215" id="mwBeQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBeU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBeY">[</span>214<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBec">]</span></span></a></sup> Since 2018 BP operates the UK's largest <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electric_vehicle" title="Electric vehicle" id="mwBeg">electric vehicle</a> charging network through its subsidiary <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/BP_Pulse" title="BP Pulse" id="mwBek">BP Pulse</a> (formerly Chargemaster).<sup about="#mwt490" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-AR18-glance_206-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"AR18-glance"}}'><a href="#cite_note-AR18-glance-206" id="mwBeo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBes"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBew">[</span>205<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBe0">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwBe4">In February 2020, BP announced a joint venture with <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/EnBW" title="EnBW" id="mwBe8">EnBW</a> to develop and operate 3<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwBfA"> </span>GW of offshore wind capacity in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crown_Estate" title="Crown Estate" id="mwBfE">Crown Estate</a> Leasing Round 4.<sup about="#mwt493" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-216" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-216"}}'><a href="#cite_note-216" id="mwBfI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBfM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBfQ">[</span>215<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBfU">]</span></span></a></sup> This is BP's first move into <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_offshore_wind_farms_in_the_United_Kingdom" title="List of offshore wind farms in the United Kingdom" id="mwBfY">Britain's offshore wind market</a>, however, BP currently provides a range of services to the offshore wind sector in the UK through its subsidiary ONYX InSight who provide a range of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Predictive_maintenance" title="Predictive maintenance" id="mwBfc">predictive maintenance</a> and engineering consultancy services to the sector.<sup about="#mwt496" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-217" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-217"}}'><a href="#cite_note-217" id="mwBfg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBfk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBfo">[</span>216<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBfs">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwBfw">In February 2022, BP announced it acquired a 30% stake in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/London" title="London" id="mwBf0">London</a>-based company, Green Biofuels Ltd, a producer of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hydrogenated_vegetable_oil" title="Hydrogenated vegetable oil" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBf4">renewable hydrogenated vegetable oil</a> fuels that can be used as a direct replacement for diesel.<sup about="#mwt499" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-218" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-218"}}'><a href="#cite_note-218" id="mwBf8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBgA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBgE">[</span>217<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBgI">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="12" id="mwBgM" aria-labelledby="United_States"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="United_States">United States</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=BP&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12" title="Edit section: United States"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwBgQ"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:BPAmericasHQ.JPG" class="mw-file-description" id="mwBgU"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:BPAmericasHQ.JPG" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/BPAmericasHQ.JPG/250px-BPAmericasHQ.JPG" decoding="async" data-file-width="2272" data-file-height="1704" data-file-type="bitmap" height="188" width="250" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/BPAmericasHQ.JPG/500px-BPAmericasHQ.JPG 2x" class="mw-file-element" id="mwBgY"/></a><figcaption id="mwBgc">The headquarters of BP America in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Westlake_Park_(Houston)" title="Westlake Park (Houston)" id="mwBgg">Westlake Park</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Houston" title="Houston" id="mwBgk">Houston</a></figcaption></figure>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwBgo"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Thunder_Horse_Semisub.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwBgs"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Thunder_Horse_Semisub.jpg" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Thunder_Horse_Semisub.jpg/250px-Thunder_Horse_Semisub.jpg" decoding="async" data-file-width="1682" data-file-height="1260" data-file-type="bitmap" height="187" width="250" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Thunder_Horse_Semisub.jpg/500px-Thunder_Horse_Semisub.jpg 2x" class="mw-file-element" id="mwBgw"/></a><figcaption id="mwBg0">The <i id="mwBg4"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thunder_Horse_PDQ" title="Thunder Horse PDQ" id="mwBg8">Thunder Horse PDQ</a></i> semi-submersible oil platform in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thunder_Horse_Oil_Field" title="Thunder Horse Oil Field" id="mwBhA">Thunder Horse Oil Field</a></figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwBhE">The United States operations comprise nearly one-third of BP's operations.<sup about="#mwt505" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-NYTBusiness2012_219-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"NYTBusiness2012"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-NYTBusiness2012-219"}}'><a href="#cite_note-NYTBusiness2012-219" id="mwBhI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBhM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBhQ">[</span>218<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBhU">]</span></span></a></sup> BP employs approximately 14,000<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwBhY"> </span>people in the United States.<sup about="#mwt506" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-AR18-USlabour_220-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"AR18-USlabour"}}'><a href="#cite_note-AR18-USlabour-220" id="mwBhc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBhg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBhk">[</span>219<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBho">]</span></span></a></sup> In 2018, BP's total production in the United States included <span about="#mwt500" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBhs" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"convert","href":"./Template:Convert"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"385000"},"2":{"wt":"oilbbl/d"}},"i":0}}]}'>385,000 barrels per day (61,200</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt500"> </span><span about="#mwt500">m</span><sup about="#mwt500">3</sup><span about="#mwt500">/d)</span> of oil and <span about="#mwt501" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBhw" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"convert","href":"./Template:Convert"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"1.9"},"2":{"wt":"e9cuft/d"},"abbr":{"wt":"off"}},"i":0}}]}'>1.9</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt501"> </span><span about="#mwt501">billion cubic feet per day (54</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt501"> </span><span about="#mwt501">million cubic metres per day)</span> of natural gas,<sup about="#mwt507" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-AR18-USproduction_221-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"AR18-USproduction"}}'><a href="#cite_note-AR18-USproduction-221" id="mwBh0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBh4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBh8">[</span>220<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBiA">]</span></span></a></sup> and its refinery throughput was <span about="#mwt502" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBiE" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"convert","href":"./Template:Convert"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"703000"},"2":{"wt":"oilbbl/d"}},"i":0}}]}'>703,000 barrels per day (111,800</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt502"> </span><span about="#mwt502">m</span><sup about="#mwt502">3</sup><span about="#mwt502">/d)</span>.<sup about="#mwt508" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-AR18-USrefinery_222-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"AR18-USrefinery"}}'><a href="#cite_note-AR18-USrefinery-222" id="mwBiI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBiM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBiQ">[</span>221<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBiU">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwBiY">BP's major subsidiary in the United States is BP America, Inc. (formerly: Standard Oil Company (Ohio) and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sohio" title="Sohio" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBic">Sohio</a>) based in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Houston,_Texas" title="Houston, Texas" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBig">Houston, Texas</a>.<sup about="#mwt509" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-biz030513_223-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"biz030513"}}'><a href="#cite_note-biz030513-223" id="mwBik"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBio"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBis">[</span>222<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBiw">]</span></span></a></sup> BP Exploration &amp; Production Inc., a 1996 established Houston-based subsidiary, is dealing with oil exploration and production.<sup about="#mwt510" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-bpexploration_224-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"bpexploration"}}'><a href="#cite_note-bpexploration-224" id="mwBi0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBi4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBi8">[</span>223<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBjA">]</span></span></a></sup> BP Corporation North America, Inc., provides petroleum refining services as also transportation fuel, heat and light energy.<sup about="#mwt511" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-bpcorporation_225-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"bpcorporation"}}'><a href="#cite_note-bpcorporation-225" id="mwBjE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBjI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBjM">[</span>224<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBjQ">]</span></span></a></sup> BP Products North America, Inc., a 1954 established Houston-based subsidiary, is engaged in the exploration, development, production, refining, and marketing of oil and natural gas.<sup about="#mwt512" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-bpproduct_226-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"bpproduct"}}'><a href="#cite_note-bpproduct-226" id="mwBjU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBjY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBjc">[</span>225<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBjg">]</span></span></a></sup> BP America Production Company, a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_Mexico" title="New Mexico" id="mwBjk">New Mexico</a>-based subsidiary, engages in oil and gas exploration and development.<sup about="#mwt513" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-bpproduction_227-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"bpproduction"}}'><a href="#cite_note-bpproduction-227" id="mwBjo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBjs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBjw">[</span>226<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBj0">]</span></span></a></sup> BP Energy Company, a Houston-based subsidiary, is a provider of natural gas, power, and risk management services to the industrial and utility sectors and a retail electric provider in Texas.<sup about="#mwt514" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-bpenergy_228-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"bpenergy"}}'><a href="#cite_note-bpenergy-228" id="mwBj4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBj8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBkA">[</span>227<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBkE">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwBkI">BP's upstream activities in the Lower 48<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwBkM"> </span>states are conducted through Denver-based BPX Energy.<sup about="#mwt517" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-denver040220_153-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"denver040220"}}'><a href="#cite_note-denver040220-153" id="mwBkQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBkU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBkY">[</span>152<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBkc">]</span></span></a></sup> It has a <span about="#mwt515" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBkg" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"convert","href":"./Template:Convert"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"7.5"},"2":{"wt":"Goilbbl"},"abbr":{"wt":"off"}},"i":0}}]}'>7.5 billion barrels (1.19</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt515"> </span><span about="#mwt515">billion cubic metres)</span> resource base on <span about="#mwt516" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBkk" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"convert","href":"./Template:Convert"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"5.7"},"2":{"wt":"e6acre"}},"i":0}}]}'>5.7</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt516"> </span><span about="#mwt516">million acres (23,000</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt516"> </span><span about="#mwt516">km</span><sup about="#mwt516">2</sup><span about="#mwt516">)</span>.<sup about="#mwt520" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-OGJ15_229-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"OGJ15"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-OGJ15-229"}}'><a href="#cite_note-OGJ15-229" id="mwBko"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBks"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBkw">[</span>228<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBk0">]</span></span></a></sup> It has <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shale_gas_in_the_United_States" title="Shale gas in the United States" id="mwBk4">shale positions</a> in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shale_gas_in_the_United_States#Woodford_Shale,_Oklahoma" title="Shale gas in the United States" id="mwBk8">Woodford, Oklahoma</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shale_gas_in_the_United_States#Haynesville_Shale,_Louisiana" title="Shale gas in the United States" id="mwBlA">Haynesville, Texas</a>, and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eagle_Ford_Formation" title="Eagle Ford Formation" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBlE">Eagle Ford, Texas</a> shales.<sup about="#mwt521" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Pulsinelli2014_230-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Pulsinelli2014"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Pulsinelli2014-230" id="mwBlI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBlM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBlQ">[</span>229<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBlU">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt522" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Rouan2012_231-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Rouan2012"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Rouan2012-231" id="mwBlY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBlc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBlg">[</span>230<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBlk">]</span></span></a></sup> It has <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Unconventional_gas" title="Unconventional gas" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBlo">unconventional gas</a> (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shale_gas" title="Shale gas" id="mwBls">shale gas</a> or <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tight_gas" title="Tight gas" id="mwBlw">tight gas</a>) stakes also in Colorado, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_Mexico" title="New Mexico" id="mwBl0">New Mexico</a> and Wyoming, primarily in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/San_Juan_Basin" title="San Juan Basin" id="mwBl4">San Juan Basin</a>.<sup about="#mwt523" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Hasterok2012_232-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Hasterok2012"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Hasterok2012-232" id="mwBl8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBmA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBmE">[</span>231<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBmI">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt524" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ZacksJun2012_233-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ZacksJun2012"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ZacksJun2012-233" id="mwBmM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBmQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBmU">[</span>232<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBmY">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt525" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-BPUSExploration_234-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"BPUSExploration"}}'><a href="#cite_note-BPUSExploration-234" id="mwBmc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBmg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBmk">[</span>233<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBmo">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwBms"><span about="#mwt526" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBmw" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"As of","href":"./Template:As_of"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"2019"}},"i":0}}]}'>As of 2019</span><sup class="plainlinks noexcerpt noprint asof-tag update" style="display:none;" about="#mwt526"><a rel="mw:ExtLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=BP&amp;action=edit" class="external text" data-mw-original-href="//en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=BP&amp;action=edit"><span typeof="mw:Entity">[</span>update<span typeof="mw:Entity">]</span></a></sup><span typeof="mw:Nowiki" about="#mwt526"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_potentially_dated_statements_from_2019" about="#mwt526"/><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:All_articles_containing_potentially_dated_statements" about="#mwt526" id="mwBm0"/>, BP produced about <span about="#mwt527" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBm4" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"convert","href":"./Template:Convert"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"300000"},"2":{"wt":"oilbbl/d"}},"i":0}}]}'>300,000 barrels per day (48,000</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt527"> </span><span about="#mwt527">m</span><sup about="#mwt527">3</sup><span about="#mwt527">/d)</span> of oil equivalent in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gulf_of_Mexico" title="Gulf of Mexico" id="mwBm8">Gulf of Mexico</a>.<sup about="#mwt530" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Ault19_235-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Ault19"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Ault19-235"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Ault19-235" id="mwBnA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBnE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBnI">[</span>234<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBnM">]</span></span></a></sup> BP operates the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Atlantis_oil_field" title="Atlantis oil field" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBnQ">Atlantis</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mad_Dog_oil_field" title="Mad Dog oil field" id="mwBnU">Mad Dog</a>, Na Kika, and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thunder_Horse_oil_field" title="Thunder Horse oil field" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBnY">Thunder Horse</a> production platforms while holding interest in hubs operated by other companies.<sup about="#mwt534" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Ambrose17_236-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Ambrose17"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Ambrose17-236"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Ambrose17-236" id="mwBnc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBng"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBnk">[</span>235<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBno">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt537" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-BP-Gulf_237-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"BP-Gulf"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-BP-Gulf-237"}}'><a href="#cite_note-BP-Gulf-237" id="mwBns"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBnw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBn0">[</span>236<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBn4">]</span></span></a></sup> In April 2023, BP launched a new oil rig, the <i id="mwBn8">Argos</i>, in the Gulf.<sup about="#mwt540" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-238" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-238"}}'><a href="#cite_note-238" id="mwBoA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBoE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBoI">[</span>237<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBoM">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwBoQ">BP operates <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Whiting_Refinery" title="Whiting Refinery" id="mwBoU">Whiting Refinery</a> in Indiana<sup about="#mwt543" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-BPUSRefining_239-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"BPUSRefining"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-BPUSRefining-239"}}'><a href="#cite_note-BPUSRefining-239" id="mwBoY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBoc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBog">[</span>238<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBok">]</span></span></a></sup> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cherry_Point_Refinery" title="Cherry Point Refinery" id="mwBoo">Cherry Point Refinery</a> in Washington.<sup about="#mwt544" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-BPUSRefining_239-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"BPUSRefining"}}'><a href="#cite_note-BPUSRefining-239" id="mwBos"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBow"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBo0">[</span>238<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBo4">]</span></span></a></sup> It formerly co-owned and operated a refinery in Toledo, Ohio, with <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Husky_Energy" title="Husky Energy" id="mwBo8">Husky Energy</a>, but sold its stake in the refinery in February 2023 to <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cenovus_Energy" title="Cenovus Energy" id="mwBpA">Cenovus Energy</a>.<sup about="#mwt547" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-240" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-240"}}'><a href="#cite_note-240" id="mwBpE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBpI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBpM">[</span>239<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBpQ">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt550" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-241" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-241"}}'><a href="#cite_note-241" id="mwBpU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBpY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBpc">[</span>240<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBpg">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt553" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-242" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-242"}}'><a href="#cite_note-242" id="mwBpk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBpo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBps">[</span>241<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBpw">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwBp0">BP operates nine onshore <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wind_farms" title="Wind farms" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBp4">wind farms</a> in six states, and held an interest in another in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hawaii" title="Hawaii" id="mwBp8">Hawaii</a> with a net generating capacity of 1,679<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwBqA"> </span>MW.<sup about="#mwt556" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-BP-wind_243-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"BP-wind"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-BP-wind-243"}}'><a href="#cite_note-BP-wind-243" id="mwBqE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBqI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBqM">[</span>242<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBqQ">]</span></span></a></sup> These wind farms include the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cedar_Creek_Wind_Farm" title="Cedar Creek Wind Farm" id="mwBqU">Cedar Creek 2</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Titan_Wind_Project" title="Titan Wind Project" id="mwBqY">Titan 1</a>, Goshen North, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flat_Ridge_Wind_Farm" title="Flat Ridge Wind Farm" id="mwBqc">Flat Ridge 1 and 2</a>, Mehoopany, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fowler_Ridge_Wind_Farm" title="Fowler Ridge Wind Farm" id="mwBqg">Fowler Ridge 1, 2 and 3</a> and Auwahi wind farms.<sup about="#mwt559" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-BP-wind-sites_244-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"BP-wind-sites"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-BP-wind-sites-244"}}'><a href="#cite_note-BP-wind-sites-244" id="mwBqk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBqo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBqs">[</span>243<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBqw">]</span></span></a></sup> It is also in process to acquire 50% non-operating stake in the Empire Wind off New York and Beacon Wind off Massachusetts offshore wind farms.<sup about="#mwt560" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-reuters100920_167-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"reuters100920"}}'><a href="#cite_note-reuters100920-167" id="mwBq0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBq4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBq8">[</span>166<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBrA">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="13" id="mwBrE" aria-labelledby="Other_locations"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="Other_locations">Other locations</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=BP&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13" title="Edit section: Other locations"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>

<p id="mwBrI">In Egypt, BP produces approximately 15% of the country's total oil production and 40% of its domestic gas.<sup about="#mwt563" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Petzet2012_245-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Petzet2012"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Petzet2012-245"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Petzet2012-245" id="mwBrM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBrQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBrU">[</span>244<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBrY">]</span></span></a></sup> The company also has offshore gas developments in the East Nile Delta Mediterranean, and in the West Nile Delta,<sup about="#mwt566" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ZacksJune2012_246-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ZacksJune2012"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-ZacksJune2012-246"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ZacksJune2012-246" id="mwBrc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBrg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBrk">[</span>245<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBro">]</span></span></a></sup> where the company has a joint investment of US$9<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwBrs"> </span>billion with <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wintershall_Dea" title="Wintershall Dea" id="mwBrw">Wintershall Dea</a> to develop North Alexandria and West Mediterranean concessions offshore gas fields.<sup about="#mwt569" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Hromadko2010_247-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Hromadko2010"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Hromadko2010-247"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Hromadko2010-247" id="mwBr0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBr4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBr8">[</span>246<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBsA">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt572" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-BPWestNile2010_248-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"BPWestNile2010"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-BPWestNile2010-248"}}'><a href="#cite_note-BPWestNile2010-248" id="mwBsE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBsI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBsM">[</span>247<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBsQ">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwBsU">BP is active in offshore oil development in Angola, where it holds an interest in a total of nine oil exploration and production blocks covering more than <span about="#mwt573" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBsY" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"convert","href":"./Template:Convert"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"30000"},"2":{"wt":"km2"}},"i":0}}]}'>30,000 square kilometres (12,000</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt573"> </span><span about="#mwt573">sq</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt573"> </span><span about="#mwt573">mi)</span>. This includes four blocks it acquired in December 2011 and an additional block that is operated by Brazilian national oil company, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Petrobras" title="Petrobras" id="mwBsc">Petrobras</a>, in which it holds a 40% stake.<sup about="#mwt576" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-BPAngolaAcquisition_249-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"BPAngolaAcquisition"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-BPAngolaAcquisition-249"}}'><a href="#cite_note-BPAngolaAcquisition-249" id="mwBsg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBsk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBso">[</span>248<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBss">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwBsw">BP has a stake in exploration of two blocks of offshore deepwater assets in the South China Sea.<sup about="#mwt579" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-China2012_250-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"China2012"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-China2012-250"}}'><a href="#cite_note-China2012-250" id="mwBs0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBs4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBs8">[</span>249<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBtA">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt582" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Xu2012_251-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Xu2012"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Xu2012-251"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Xu2012-251" id="mwBtE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBtI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBtM">[</span>250<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBtQ">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwBtU">In India, BP owns a 30% share of oil and gas assets operated by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reliance_Industries" title="Reliance Industries" id="mwBtY">Reliance Industries</a>, including exploration and production rights in more than 20<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwBtc"> </span>offshore oil and gas blocks, representing an investment of more than US$7<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwBtg"> </span>billion into oil and gas exploration in the country.<sup about="#mwt585" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Sharma2011_252-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Sharma2011"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Sharma2011-252"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Sharma2011-252" id="mwBtk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBto"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBts">[</span>251<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBtw">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwBt0">BP has major liquefied natural gas activities in Indonesia, where it operates the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tangguh_gas_field" title="Tangguh gas field" id="mwBt4">Tangguh LNG</a> project, which began production in 2009 and has a capacity of 7.6<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwBt8"> </span>million tonnes of liquid natural gas per year.<sup about="#mwt588" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Grieder2009_253-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Grieder2009"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Grieder2009-253"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Grieder2009-253" id="mwBuA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBuE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBuI">[</span>252<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBuM">]</span></span></a></sup> In 2025, BP signed three addional production sharing contracts for the Bintuni, Drawa, and Barong blocks, increasing the company's total participation in Indonesia to 11 oil and gas blocks.<sup about="#mwt591" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-o&amp;g_254-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"o&amp;g"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-o&amp;g-254"}}'><a href="#cite_note-o&amp;g-254" id="mwBuQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBuU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBuY">[</span>253<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBuc">]</span></span></a></sup> Also in that country, the company has invested in the exploration and development of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coalbed_methane" title="Coalbed methane" id="mwBug">coalbed methane</a>.<sup about="#mwt592" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Suhana2011_255-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Suhana2011"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Suhana2011-255" id="mwBuk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBuo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBus">[</span>254<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBuw">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwBu0">BP operates in Iraq as part of the joint venture <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rumaila_Field_Operating_Organization" title="Rumaila Field Operating Organization" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBu4">Rumaila Operating Organization</a> in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rumaila_oil_field" title="Rumaila oil field" id="mwBu8">Rumaila oil field</a>, the world's fourth largest oilfield, where it produced over <span about="#mwt593" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBvA" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"convert","href":"./Template:Convert"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"1"},"2":{"wt":"Moilbbl/d"}},"i":0}}]}'>1 million barrels per day (160</span><span style="margin-left:0.2em" about="#mwt593">×<span style="margin-left:0.1em">10</span></span><s style="display:none" about="#mwt593">^</s><sup about="#mwt593">3</sup><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt593"> </span><span about="#mwt593">m</span><sup about="#mwt593">3</sup><span about="#mwt593">/d)</span> of oil equivalent in 2011.<sup about="#mwt596" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ReutersOct2009_256-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ReutersOct2009"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-ReutersOct2009-256"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ReutersOct2009-256" id="mwBvE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBvI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBvM">[</span>255<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBvQ">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt599" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-UPIJan11_257-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"UPIJan11"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-UPIJan11-257"}}'><a href="#cite_note-UPIJan11-257" id="mwBvU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBvY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBvc">[</span>256<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBvg">]</span></span></a></sup> A BBC investigation found in 2022 that waste-gas was being burned as close as 350 meters from people's homes. A leaked report from <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ministry_of_Health_(Iraq)" title="Ministry of Health (Iraq)" id="mwBvk">Ministry of Health (Iraq)</a> blamed <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Air_pollution" title="Air pollution" id="mwBvo">air pollution</a> for 20% rise in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cancer" title="Cancer" id="mwBvs">cancer</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Basra" title="Basra" id="mwBvw">Basra</a> between 2015 and 2018.<sup about="#mwt600" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-BBC1_258-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"BBC1"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-BBC1-258"}}'><a href="#cite_note-BBC1-258" id="mwBv0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBv4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBv8">[</span>257<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBwA">]</span></span></a></sup> The Iraqi Ministry of Health has banned its employees from speaking about the health damage.<sup about="#mwt601" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-BBC1_258-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"BBC1"}}'><a href="#cite_note-BBC1-258" id="mwBwE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBwI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBwM">[</span>257<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBwQ">]</span></span></a></sup> Iraqi Environment Minister Jassem al-Falahi later admitted that "pollution from oil production is the main reason for increases in local cancer rates."<sup about="#mwt604" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-259" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-259"}}'><a href="#cite_note-259" id="mwBwU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBwY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBwc">[</span>258<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBwg">]</span></span></a></sup> In February 2025, BP signed a $25 billion deal to redevelop four oil and gas fields in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kirkuk" title="Kirkuk" id="mwBwk">Kirkuk</a>, Iraq.<sup about="#mwt607" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-260" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-260"}}'><a href="#cite_note-260" id="mwBwo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBws"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBww">[</span>259<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBw0">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt610" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-261" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-261"}}'><a href="#cite_note-261" id="mwBw4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBw8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBxA">[</span>260<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBxE">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwBxI">In Oman, BP currently has a 60% participation interest in Block 61. Block 61 is one of Oman's largest gas blocks with a daily production capacity of 1.5 billion cubic feet of gas and more than 65,000 barrels of condensate. It covers around 3,950<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwBxM"> </span>km in central Oman and contains the largest tight gas development in the Middle East. On 1 February 2021, BP inked a deal to sell 20% participating interest in Block 61 to Thailand's <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/PTT_Exploration_and_Production" title="PTT Exploration and Production" id="mwBxQ">PTT Exploration and Production Public Company Ltd. (PTTEP)</a> for a total of $2.6 billion. Upon closure of the sale, the BP will remain the block's operator with a 40% interest.<sup about="#mwt613" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-262" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-262"}}'><a href="#cite_note-262" id="mwBxU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBxY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBxc">[</span>261<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBxg">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt616" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-263" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-263"}}'><a href="#cite_note-263" id="mwBxk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBxo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBxs">[</span>262<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBxw">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwBx0"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Australian_road_train_headed_by_Volvo_NH15.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwBx4"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Australian_road_train_headed_by_Volvo_NH15.jpg" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Australian_road_train_headed_by_Volvo_NH15.jpg/250px-Australian_road_train_headed_by_Volvo_NH15.jpg" decoding="async" data-file-width="3388" data-file-height="2192" data-file-type="bitmap" height="162" width="250" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Australian_road_train_headed_by_Volvo_NH15.jpg/500px-Australian_road_train_headed_by_Volvo_NH15.jpg 2x" class="mw-file-element" id="mwBx8"/></a><figcaption id="mwByA">A BP <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Road_train" title="Road train" id="mwByE">road train</a> in the Australian outback</figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwByI">Prior to March 2021, BP operated the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kwinana_Oil_Refinery" title="Kwinana Oil Refinery" id="mwByM">Kwinana</a> refinery in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Western_Australia" title="Western Australia" id="mwByQ">Western Australia</a>, which was the country's largest refinery,<sup about="#mwt620" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Denton15_264-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Denton15"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Denton15-264"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Denton15-264" id="mwByU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwByY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwByc">[</span>263<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwByg">]</span></span></a></sup> supplying about 70% of Western Australia's fuel needs. The former refinery, located on <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cockburn_Sound" title="Cockburn Sound" id="mwByk">Cockburn Sound</a>, was <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kwinana_Oil_Refinery#Conversion_to_import_terminal" title="Kwinana Oil Refinery" id="mwByo">converted</a> to an import terminal and, <span about="#mwt617" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBys" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"As of","href":"./Template:As_of"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"2025"},"lc":{"wt":"y"}},"i":0}}]}'>as of 2025</span><sup class="plainlinks noexcerpt noprint asof-tag update" style="display:none;" about="#mwt617"><a rel="mw:ExtLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=BP&amp;action=edit" class="external text" data-mw-original-href="//en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=BP&amp;action=edit"><span typeof="mw:Entity">[</span>update<span typeof="mw:Entity">]</span></a></sup><span typeof="mw:Nowiki" about="#mwt617"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_potentially_dated_statements_from_2025" about="#mwt617"/><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:All_articles_containing_potentially_dated_statements" about="#mwt617" id="mwByw"/>, was transitioning into a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Biorefinery" title="Biorefinery" id="mwBy0">biorefinery</a> and green hydrogen production facility.<sup about="#mwt623" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-265" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-265"}}'><a href="#cite_note-265" id="mwBy4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBy8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBzA">[</span>264<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBzE">]</span></span></a></sup> But in 2025 BP announced it was ending its role in producing hydrogen in the region.<sup about="#mwt626" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-266" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-266"}}'><a href="#cite_note-266" id="mwBzI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBzM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBzQ">[</span>265<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBzU">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwBzY">BP is a non-operating joint venture partner in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/North_West_Shelf" title="North West Shelf" id="mwBzc">North West Shelf</a>, which produces LNG, pipeline gas, condensate and oil.<sup about="#mwt629" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Chambers16_267-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Chambers16"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Chambers16-267"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Chambers16-267" id="mwBzg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBzk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBzo">[</span>266<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBzs">]</span></span></a></sup> The NWS venture is Australia's largest resource development and accounts for around one third of Australia's oil and gas production.<sup about="#mwt632" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Lanis17_268-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Lanis17"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Lanis17-268"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Lanis17-268" id="mwBzw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBz0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBz4">[</span>267<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBz8">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt635" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Daiss16_269-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Daiss16"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Daiss16-269"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Daiss16-269" id="mwB0A"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB0E"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB0I">[</span>268<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB0M">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwB0Q">BP operates the two largest oil and gas production projects in the Azerbaijan's sector of the Caspian Sea, the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Azeri–Chirag–Guneshli" title="Azeri–Chirag–Guneshli" class="mw-redirect" id="mwB0U">Azeri–Chirag–Guneshli</a> offshore oil fields, which supplies 80% of the country's oil production, and the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shah_Deniz_gas_field" title="Shah Deniz gas field" id="mwB0Y">Shah Deniz gas field</a>. It also and develops the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shafag-Asiman" title="Shafag-Asiman" class="mw-redirect" id="mwB0c">Shafag-Asiman</a> complex of offshore geological structures.<sup about="#mwt638" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Neff2010_270-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Neff2010"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Neff2010-270"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Neff2010-270" id="mwB0g"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB0k"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB0o">[</span>269<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB0s">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt641" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Yevgrashina2012_271-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Yevgrashina2012"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Yevgrashina2012-271"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Yevgrashina2012-271" id="mwB0w"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB00"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB04">[</span>270<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB08">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt644" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-today_272-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"today"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-today-272"}}'><a href="#cite_note-today-272" id="mwB1A"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB1E"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB1I">[</span>271<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB1M">]</span></span></a></sup> In addition, it operates the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sangachal_Terminal" title="Sangachal Terminal" id="mwB1Q">Sangachal terminal</a> and the Azerbaijan's major export pipelines through <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Georgia_(country)" title="Georgia (country)" id="mwB1U">Georgia</a> such as <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baku–Tbilisi–Ceyhan_pipeline" title="Baku–Tbilisi–Ceyhan pipeline" id="mwB1Y">Baku–Tbilisi–Ceyhan</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baku–Supsa_Pipeline" title="Baku–Supsa Pipeline" id="mwB1c">Baku–Supsa</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/South_Caucasus_Pipeline" title="South Caucasus Pipeline" id="mwB1g">South Caucasus</a> pipelines.<sup about="#mwt647" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-273" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-273"}}'><a href="#cite_note-273" id="mwB1k"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB1o"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB1s">[</span>272<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB1w">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<figure class="mw-default-size mw-halign-right" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwB10"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Oil_depot,_Frontignan,_Hérault_01.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwB14"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Oil_depot,_Frontignan,_Hérault_01.jpg" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Oil_depot%2C_Frontignan%2C_H%C3%A9rault_01.jpg/250px-Oil_depot%2C_Frontignan%2C_H%C3%A9rault_01.jpg" decoding="async" data-file-width="4882" data-file-height="3051" data-file-type="bitmap" height="156" width="250" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Oil_depot%2C_Frontignan%2C_H%C3%A9rault_01.jpg/500px-Oil_depot%2C_Frontignan%2C_H%C3%A9rault_01.jpg 2x" class="mw-file-element" id="mwB18"/></a><figcaption id="mwB2A">A GDH (subsidiary of BP) oil depot, Frontigan, Hérault, France</figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwB2E">BP's refining operations in continental Europe include Europe's second-largest oil refinery, located in Rotterdam, the Netherlands, which can process up to <span about="#mwt648" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwB2I" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"convert","href":"./Template:Convert"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"377000"},"2":{"wt":"oilbbl"}},"i":0}}]}'>377,000 barrels (59,900</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt648"> </span><span about="#mwt648">m</span><sup about="#mwt648">3</sup><span about="#mwt648">)</span> of crude oil per day.<sup about="#mwt649" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Reuters2009_274-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Reuters2009"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Reuters2009-274" id="mwB2M"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB2Q"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB2U">[</span>273<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB2Y">]</span></span></a></sup> Other facilities are located in Ingolstadt, Gelsenkirchen and Lingen, in Germany, as well as one in Castellón, Spain.<sup about="#mwt653" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-275" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-275"}}'><a href="#cite_note-275" id="mwB2c"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB2g"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB2k">[</span>274<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB2o">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwB2s">In addition to its offshore operations in the British zone of North Sea, BP has interests in the Norwegian section of the sea through its stake in Aker BP. <span about="#mwt654" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwB2w" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"As of","href":"./Template:As_of"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"2018"},"2":{"wt":"12"}},"i":0}}]}'>As of December</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt654"> </span><span about="#mwt654">2018</span><sup class="plainlinks noexcerpt noprint asof-tag update" style="display:none;" about="#mwt654"><a rel="mw:ExtLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=BP&amp;action=edit" class="external text" data-mw-original-href="//en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=BP&amp;action=edit"><span typeof="mw:Entity">[</span>update<span typeof="mw:Entity">]</span></a></sup><span typeof="mw:Nowiki" about="#mwt654"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_potentially_dated_statements_from_December_2018" about="#mwt654"/><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:All_articles_containing_potentially_dated_statements" about="#mwt654" id="mwB20"/>, BP holds a 19.75% stake in Russia's state-controlled oil company Rosneft.<sup about="#mwt655" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:2_133-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":2"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:2-133" id="mwB24"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB28"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB3A">[</span>132<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB3E">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt656" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-reuters220313_135-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"reuters220313"}}'><a href="#cite_note-reuters220313-135" id="mwB3I"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB3M"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB3Q">[</span>134<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB3U">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt657" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-AR18-Rosneft_276-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"AR18-Rosneft"}}'><a href="#cite_note-AR18-Rosneft-276" id="mwB3Y"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB3c"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB3g">[</span>275<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB3k">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwB3o">Retail operations of motor vehicle fuels in Europe are present in the United Kingdom, France, Germany (through the Aral brand), the Netherlands, Switzerland, Italy, Austria, Poland, Portugal, Greece and Turkey.<sup about="#mwt660" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-277" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-277"}}'><a href="#cite_note-277" id="mwB3s"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB3w"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB30">[</span>276<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB34">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt663" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-278" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-278"}}'><a href="#cite_note-278" id="mwB38"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB4A"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB4E">[</span>277<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB4I">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt666" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-279" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-279"}}'><a href="#cite_note-279" id="mwB4M"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB4Q"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB4U">[</span>278<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB4Y">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwB4c">BP's Canadian operations are headquartered in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Calgary" title="Calgary" id="mwB4g">Calgary</a> and the company operates primarily in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Newfoundland" title="Newfoundland" class="mw-redirect" id="mwB4k">Newfoundland</a>.<sup about="#mwt669" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-280" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-280"}}'><a href="#cite_note-280" id="mwB4o"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB4s"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB4w">[</span>279<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB40">]</span></span></a></sup> It purchases crude oil for the company's refineries in the United States, and has a 35 per cent stake in the undeveloped Bay du Nord project and three offshore exploration block in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Newfoundland" title="Newfoundland" class="mw-redirect" id="mwB44">Newfoundland</a>.<sup about="#mwt672" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-upstream1611112_281-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"upstream1611112"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-upstream1611112-281"}}'><a href="#cite_note-upstream1611112-281" id="mwB48"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB5A"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB5E">[</span>280<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB5I">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwB5M">BP is the largest oil and gas producer in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trinidad_and_Tobago" title="Trinidad and Tobago" id="mwB5Q">Trinidad and Tobago</a>, where it holds more than <span about="#mwt673" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwB5U" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"convert","href":"./Template:Convert"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"1350"},"2":{"wt":"km2"}},"i":0}}]}'>1,350 square kilometres (520</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt673"> </span><span about="#mwt673">sq</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt673"> </span><span about="#mwt673">mi)</span> of offshore assets and is the largest shareholder in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Atlantic_LNG" title="Atlantic LNG" id="mwB5Y">Atlantic LNG</a>, one of the largest <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/LNG_plant" title="LNG plant" class="mw-redirect" id="mwB5c">LNG plants</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Western_Hemisphere" title="Western Hemisphere" id="mwB5g">Western Hemisphere</a>.<sup about="#mwt676" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-UPIMay11_282-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"UPIMay11"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-UPIMay11-282"}}'><a href="#cite_note-UPIMay11-282" id="mwB5k"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB5o"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB5s">[</span>281<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB5w">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwB50">In Brazil, BP holds stakes in offshore oil and gas exploration in the Barreirinhas, Ceará and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Campos_Basin" title="Campos Basin" id="mwB54">Campos</a> basins, in addition to onshore processing facilities.<sup about="#mwt679" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Flynn2012_283-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Flynn2012"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Flynn2012-283"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Flynn2012-283" id="mwB58"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB6A"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB6E">[</span>282<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB6I">]</span></span></a></sup> BP also operates biofuel production facilities in Brazil, including three cane sugar mills for ethanol production.<sup about="#mwt682" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Fick2011_284-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Fick2011"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Fick2011-284"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Fick2011-284" id="mwB6M"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB6Q"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB6U">[</span>283<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB6Y">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt683" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-reuters140911_285-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"reuters140911"}}'><a href="#cite_note-reuters140911-285" id="mwB6c"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB6g"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB6k">[</span>284<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB6o">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwB6s">BP operated in Singapore until 2004 when it sold its retail network of 28 stations and LPG business to <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Singapore_Petroleum_Company" title="Singapore Petroleum Company" id="mwB6w">Singapore Petroleum Company</a> (SPC). It also sold its 50% in SPC.<sup about="#mwt686" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-286" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-286"}}'><a href="#cite_note-286" id="mwB60"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB64"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB68">[</span>285<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB7A">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwB7E">BP has a significant presence in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/South_Africa" title="South Africa" id="mwB7I">South Africa</a>, operating refineries and 500 gas stations across the country.<sup about="#mwt689" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Shell_kisses_South_African_service_stations_and_refinery_goodbye_287-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Shell kisses South African service stations and refinery goodbye"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Shell_kisses_South_African_service_stations_and_refinery_goodbye-287"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Shell_kisses_South_African_service_stations_and_refinery_goodbye-287" id="mwB7M"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB7Q"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB7U">[</span>286<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB7Y">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section></section><section data-mw-section-id="14" id="mwB7c" aria-labelledby="Exploration_and_production"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Exploration_and_production">Exploration and production</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=BP&amp;action=edit&amp;section=14" title="Edit section: Exploration and production"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt690" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwB7g" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"See also","href":"./Template:See_also"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Oil fields operated by BP"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1353705441" about="#mwt691" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt690" id="mwB7k">See also: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oil_fields_operated_by_BP" title="Oil fields operated by BP">Oil fields operated by BP</a></div>
<p id="mwB7o">BP Upstream's activities include exploring for new oil and natural gas resources, developing access to such resources, and producing, transporting, storing and processing oil and natural gas.<sup about="#mwt698" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Forbes2012_288-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Forbes2012"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Forbes2012-288" id="mwB7s"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB7w"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB70">[</span>287<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB74">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt699" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-CNNMoney2011_289-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"CNNMoney2011"}}'><a href="#cite_note-CNNMoney2011-289" id="mwB78"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB8A"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB8E">[</span>288<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB8I">]</span></span></a></sup> The activities in this area of operations take place in 25<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwB8M"> </span>countries worldwide. In 2018, BP produced around <span about="#mwt692" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwB8Q" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"convert","href":"./Template:Convert"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"3.7"},"2":{"wt":"Moilbbl/d"}},"i":0}}]}'>3.7 million barrels per day (590</span><span style="margin-left:0.2em" about="#mwt692">×<span style="margin-left:0.1em">10</span></span><s style="display:none" about="#mwt692">^</s><sup about="#mwt692">3</sup><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt692"> </span><span about="#mwt692">m</span><sup about="#mwt692">3</sup><span about="#mwt692">/d)</span> of oil equivalent,<sup about="#mwt700" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-AR18-glance_206-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"AR18-glance"}}'><a href="#cite_note-AR18-glance-206" id="mwB8U"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB8Y"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB8c">[</span>205<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB8g">]</span></span></a></sup> of which <span about="#mwt693" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwB8k" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"convert","href":"./Template:Convert"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"2.191"},"2":{"wt":"Moilbbl/d"}},"i":0}}]}'>2.191 million barrels per day (348.3</span><span style="margin-left:0.2em" about="#mwt693">×<span style="margin-left:0.1em">10</span></span><s style="display:none" about="#mwt693">^</s><sup about="#mwt693">3</sup><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt693"> </span><span about="#mwt693">m</span><sup about="#mwt693">3</sup><span about="#mwt693">/d)</span> were liquids and <span about="#mwt694" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwB8o" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"convert","href":"./Template:Convert"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"8.659"},"2":{"wt":"e9cuft/d"},"abbr":{"wt":"off"}},"i":0}}]}'>8.659</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt694"> </span><span about="#mwt694">billion cubic feet per day (245.2</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt694"> </span><span about="#mwt694">million cubic metres per day)</span> was natural gas, and had total proved reserves of <span about="#mwt695" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwB8s" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"convert","href":"./Template:Convert"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"19945"},"2":{"wt":"Moilbbl"}},"i":0}}]}'>19,945 million barrels (3,171.0</span><span style="margin-left:0.2em" about="#mwt695">×<span style="margin-left:0.1em">10</span></span><s style="display:none" about="#mwt695">^</s><sup about="#mwt695">6</sup><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt695"> </span><span about="#mwt695">m</span><sup about="#mwt695">3</sup><span about="#mwt695">)</span> of oil equivalent, of which liquids accounted <span about="#mwt696" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwB8w" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"convert","href":"./Template:Convert"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"11456"},"2":{"wt":"Moilbbl"}},"i":0}}]}'>11,456 million barrels (1,821.4</span><span style="margin-left:0.2em" about="#mwt696">×<span style="margin-left:0.1em">10</span></span><s style="display:none" about="#mwt696">^</s><sup about="#mwt696">6</sup><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt696"> </span><span about="#mwt696">m</span><sup about="#mwt696">3</sup><span about="#mwt696">)</span> barrels and natural gas <span about="#mwt697" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwB80" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"convert","href":"./Template:Convert"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"49.239"},"2":{"wt":"e12cuft"},"abbr":{"wt":"off"}},"i":0}}]}'>49.239</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt697"> </span><span about="#mwt697">trillion cubic feet (1.3943</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt697"> </span><span about="#mwt697">trillion cubic metres)</span>.<sup about="#mwt701" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-AR18-estimates_290-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"AR18-estimates"}}'><a href="#cite_note-AR18-estimates-290" id="mwB84"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB88"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB9A">[</span>289<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB9E">]</span></span></a></sup> In addition to the conventional oil exploration and production, BP has a stake in the three oil sands projects in Canada.<sup about="#mwt702" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-fp300712_116-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"fp300712"}}'><a href="#cite_note-fp300712-116" id="mwB9I"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB9M"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB9Q">[</span>115<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB9U">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt703" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-reuters240620_291-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"reuters240620"}}'><a href="#cite_note-reuters240620-291" id="mwB9Y"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB9c"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB9g">[</span>290<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB9k">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwB9o">BP had plans to drop its oil and gas production to fall by at least one million barrels a day by 2030, a 40% reduction on 2019 levels, but this was scrapped in October 2024, with plans for an increase in production instead.<sup about="#mwt706" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:4_292-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":4"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-:4-292"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:4-292" id="mwB9s"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB9w"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB90">[</span>291<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB94">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt707" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-cnn040820_293-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"cnn040820"}}'><a href="#cite_note-cnn040820-293" id="mwB98"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB-A"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB-E">[</span>292<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB-I">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="15" id="mwB-M" aria-labelledby="Refining_and_marketing"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Refining_and_marketing">Refining and marketing</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=BP&amp;action=edit&amp;section=15" title="Edit section: Refining and marketing"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwB-Q"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Aral.JPG" class="mw-file-description" id="mwB-U"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Aral.JPG" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Aral.JPG/250px-Aral.JPG" decoding="async" data-file-width="800" data-file-height="536" data-file-type="bitmap" height="168" width="250" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Aral.JPG/500px-Aral.JPG 2x" class="mw-file-element" id="mwB-Y"/></a><figcaption id="mwB-c">An <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aral_AG" title="Aral AG" id="mwB-g">Aral</a> service station in Weiterstadt, Germany</figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwB-k">BP downstream's activities include the refining, marketing, manufacturing, transportation, trading and supply of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crude_oil" title="Crude oil" class="mw-redirect" id="mwB-o">crude oil</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Petroleum_product" title="Petroleum product" id="mwB-s">petroleum products</a>.<sup about="#mwt708" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Forbes2012_288-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Forbes2012"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Forbes2012-288" id="mwB-w"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB-0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB-4">[</span>287<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB-8">]</span></span></a></sup> Downstream is responsible for BP's fuels and lubricants businesses, and has major operations located in Europe, North America and Asia.<sup about="#mwt711" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ReutersProfile2012_294-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ReutersProfile2012"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-ReutersProfile2012-294"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ReutersProfile2012-294" id="mwB_A"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB_E"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB_I">[</span>293<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB_M">]</span></span></a></sup> As of 2018, BP owned or had a share in 11<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwB_Q"> </span>refineries.<sup about="#mwt712" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-AR18-USrefinery_222-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"AR18-USrefinery"}}'><a href="#cite_note-AR18-USrefinery-222" id="mwB_U"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB_Y"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB_c">[</span>221<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB_g">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwB_k">BP, which employs about 1,800<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwB_o"> </span>people in oil trading and trades over <span about="#mwt713" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwB_s" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"convert","href":"./Template:Convert"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"5"},"2":{"wt":"Moilbbl/d"}},"i":0}}]}'>5 million barrels per day (790</span><span style="margin-left:0.2em" about="#mwt713">×<span style="margin-left:0.1em">10</span></span><s style="display:none" about="#mwt713">^</s><sup about="#mwt713">3</sup><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt713"> </span><span about="#mwt713">m</span><sup about="#mwt713">3</sup><span about="#mwt713">/d)</span> of oil and refined products, is the world's third-biggest oil trader after <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Royal_Dutch_Shell" title="Royal Dutch Shell" class="mw-redirect" id="mwB_w">Royal Dutch Shell</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vitol" title="Vitol" id="mwB_0">Vitol</a>.<sup about="#mwt714" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Reuters_BP_trading_295-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Reuters BP trading"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Reuters_BP_trading-295" id="mwB_4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB_8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCAA">[</span>294<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCAE">]</span></span></a></sup> The operation is estimated to be able to generate over $1<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwCAI"> </span>billion trading profits in a good year.<sup about="#mwt717" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Reuters_BP_trading_295-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Reuters BP trading"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Reuters_BP_trading-295"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Reuters_BP_trading-295" id="mwCAM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCAQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCAU">[</span>294<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCAY">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwCAc"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Air_BP" title="Air BP" id="mwCAg">Air BP</a> is the aviation division of BP, providing <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aviation_fuel" title="Aviation fuel" id="mwCAk">aviation fuel</a>, lubricants &amp; services. It has operations in over 50<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwCAo"> </span>countries worldwide. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/BP_Shipping" title="BP Shipping" id="mwCAs">BP Shipping</a> provides the logistics to move BP's oil and gas cargoes to market, as well as marine structural assurance.<sup about="#mwt720" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-296" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-296"}}'><a href="#cite_note-296" id="mwCAw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCA0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCA4">[</span>295<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCA8">]</span></span></a></sup> It manages a large fleet of vessels most of which are held on long-term operating leases. BP Shipping's chartering teams based in London, Singapore, and Chicago also charter third party vessels on both time charter and voyage charter basis. The BP-managed fleet consists of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Very_Large_Crude_Carrier" title="Very Large Crude Carrier" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCBA">Very Large Crude Carriers</a> (VLCCs), one North Sea shuttle tanker, medium size crude and product carriers, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/LNG_carrier" title="LNG carrier" id="mwCBE">liquefied natural gas (LNG) carriers</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/LPG_carrier" title="LPG carrier" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCBI">liquefied petroleum gas (LPG) carriers</a>, and coasters. All of these ships are double-hulled.<sup about="#mwt723" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-297" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-297"}}'><a href="#cite_note-297" id="mwCBM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCBQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCBU">[</span>296<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCBY">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwCBc">BP has around 18,700<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwCBg"> </span>service stations worldwide.<sup about="#mwt724" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-AR18-glance_206-3" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"AR18-glance"}}'><a href="#cite_note-AR18-glance-206" id="mwCBk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCBo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCBs">[</span>205<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCBw">]</span></span></a></sup> Its flagship retail brand is BP Connect, a chain of service stations combined with a convenience store,<sup about="#mwt727" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-BPServiceStations_298-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"BPServiceStations"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-BPServiceStations-298"}}'><a href="#cite_note-BPServiceStations-298" id="mwCB0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCB4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCB8">[</span>297<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCCA">]</span></span></a></sup> although in the US it is gradually being transitioned to the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ampm" title="Ampm" id="mwCCE">ampm</a> format. BP also owns half of Kentucky-based convenience store company <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thorntons_LLC" title="Thorntons LLC" id="mwCCI">Thorntons LLC</a> with ArcLight Capital Partners (who own the Gulf brand in the United States) since 2019. On 13 July 2021, BP announced it will take acquire ArcLight Capital Partners' share of Thorntons, and thus fully own the convenience store company. The deal is expected to close later in the year.<sup about="#mwt730" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-299" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-299"}}'><a href="#cite_note-299" id="mwCCM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCCQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCCU">[</span>298<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCCY">]</span></span></a></sup> In Germany and Luxembourg, BP operates service stations under the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aral_AG" title="Aral AG" id="mwCCc">Aral</a> brand.<sup about="#mwt733" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-BPAral_98-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"BPAral"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-BPAral-98"}}'><a href="#cite_note-BPAral-98" id="mwCCg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCCk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCCo">[</span>97<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCCs">]</span></span></a></sup> On the US West Coast, in the states of California, Oregon, Washington, Nevada, Idaho, Arizona, and Utah, BP primarily operates service stations under the ARCO brand.<sup about="#mwt736" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-BPArco_300-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"BPArco"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-BPArco-300"}}'><a href="#cite_note-BPArco-300" id="mwCCw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCC0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCC4">[</span>299<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCC8">]</span></span></a></sup> In Australia BP operates a number of BP Travel Centres, large-scale destination sites located which, in addition to the usual facilities in a BP Connect site, also feature food-retail tenants such as <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/McDonald's" title="McDonald's" id="mwCDA">McDonald's</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/KFC" title="KFC" id="mwCDE">KFC</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nando's" title="Nando's" id="mwCDI">Nando's</a> and facilities for long-haul truck drivers.<sup about="#mwt739" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-BP_Truck_Stop_Australia_301-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"BP Truck Stop Australia"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-BP_Truck_Stop_Australia-301"}}'><a href="#cite_note-BP_Truck_Stop_Australia-301" id="mwCDM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCDQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCDU">[</span>300<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCDY">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwCDc"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Castrol" title="Castrol" id="mwCDg">Castrol</a> is BP's main brand for industrial and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Automotive" title="Automotive" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCDk">automotive</a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lubricants" title="Lubricants" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCDo">lubricants</a> and is applied to a large range of BP oils, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grease_(lubricant)" title="Grease (lubricant)" id="mwCDs">greases</a> and similar products for most <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lubrication" title="Lubrication" id="mwCDw">lubrication</a> applications.<sup about="#mwt742" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-BPCastrol_302-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"BPCastrol"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-BPCastrol-302"}}'><a href="#cite_note-BPCastrol-302" id="mwCD0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCD4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCD8">[</span>301<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCEA">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="16" id="mwCEE" aria-labelledby="Clean_energy"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Clean_energy">Clean energy</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=BP&amp;action=edit&amp;section=16" title="Edit section: Clean energy"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<figure class="mw-default-size mw-halign-right" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwCEI"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:SolarpanelBp.JPG" class="mw-file-description" id="mwCEM"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:SolarpanelBp.JPG" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/SolarpanelBp.JPG/250px-SolarpanelBp.JPG" decoding="async" data-file-width="532" data-file-height="299" data-file-type="bitmap" height="141" width="250" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/SolarpanelBp.JPG/500px-SolarpanelBp.JPG 2x" class="mw-file-element" id="mwCEQ"/></a><figcaption id="mwCEU">A BP photovoltaic (PV) module that is composed of multiple PV cells. Two or more interconnected PV modules create an array.</figcaption></figure>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwCEY"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Fowler_Ridge_Wind_Farm_2621902438.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwCEc"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Fowler_Ridge_Wind_Farm_2621902438.jpg" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Fowler_Ridge_Wind_Farm_2621902438.jpg/250px-Fowler_Ridge_Wind_Farm_2621902438.jpg" decoding="async" data-file-width="3880" data-file-height="2607" data-file-type="bitmap" height="168" width="250" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Fowler_Ridge_Wind_Farm_2621902438.jpg/500px-Fowler_Ridge_Wind_Farm_2621902438.jpg 2x" class="mw-file-element" id="mwCEg"/></a><figcaption id="mwCEk">The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fowler_Ridge_Wind_Farm" title="Fowler Ridge Wind Farm" id="mwCEo">Fowler Ridge Wind Farm</a></figcaption></figure>

<p id="mwCEs">BP's public rhetoric and pledges emphasise that the company is shifting towards climate-friendly, low-carbon and transition strategies. However, a 2022 study found that the company's spending on clean energy was insignificant and opaque, with little to suggest that the company's discourse matched its actions.<sup about="#mwt745" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-303" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-303"}}'><a href="#cite_note-303" id="mwCEw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCE0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCE4">[</span>302<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCE8">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwCFA">BP was the first of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Supermajor" title="Supermajor" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCFE">supermajors</a> to say that it would focus on energy sources other than fossil fuels.<sup about="#mwt746" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-reuters151217_150-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"reuters151217"}}'><a href="#cite_note-reuters151217-150" id="mwCFI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCFM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCFQ">[</span>149<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCFU">]</span></span></a></sup> It established an <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alternative_energy" title="Alternative energy" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCFY">alternative</a> and low carbon energy business in 2005. According to the company, it spent a total of $8.3<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwCFc"> </span>billion in renewable energy projects including solar, wind, and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Biofuels" title="Biofuels" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCFg">biofuels</a>, and non-renewable projects including <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Natural_gas" title="Natural gas" id="mwCFk">natural gas</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hydrogen_power" title="Hydrogen power" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCFo">hydrogen power</a>, through completion in 2013.<sup about="#mwt747" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Schiller-2012_304-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Schiller-2012"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Schiller-2012-304" id="mwCFs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCFw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCF0">[</span>303<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCF4">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt748" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Wells2012_305-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Wells2012"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Wells2012-305" id="mwCF8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCGA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCGE">[</span>304<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCGI">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt749" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-sieber151217_306-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"sieber151217"}}'><a href="#cite_note-sieber151217-306" id="mwCGM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCGQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCGU">[</span>305<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCGY">]</span></span></a></sup> The relatively small size of BP's alternative energy operations has led to allegations of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greenwashing" title="Greenwashing" id="mwCGc">greenwashing</a> by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greenpeace" title="Greenpeace" id="mwCGg">Greenpeace</a>,<sup about="#mwt750" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-greenpeace211010_307-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"greenpeace211010"}}'><a href="#cite_note-greenpeace211010-307" id="mwCGk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCGo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCGs">[</span>306<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCGw">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mother_Jones_(magazine)" title="Mother Jones (magazine)" id="mwCG0">Mother Jones</a>,<sup about="#mwt751" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-motherjones040510_308-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"motherjones040510"}}'><a href="#cite_note-motherjones040510-308" id="mwCG4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCG8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCHA">[</span>307<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCHE">]</span></span></a></sup> and energy analyst and activist <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Antonia_Juhasz" title="Antonia Juhasz" id="mwCHI">Antonia Juhasz</a>,<sup about="#mwt752" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-accuracy210812_309-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"accuracy210812"}}'><a href="#cite_note-accuracy210812-309" id="mwCHM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCHQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCHU">[</span>308<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCHY">]</span></span></a></sup> among others.<sup about="#mwt753" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-guardian201108_310-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"guardian201108"}}'><a href="#cite_note-guardian201108-310" id="mwCHc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCHg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCHk">[</span>309<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCHo">]</span></span></a></sup> In 2018, the CEO Bob Dudley said that out of the company's total spending of $15 to $17<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwCHs"> </span>billion per year, about $500<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwCHw"> </span>million will be invested in low-carbon energy and technology.<sup about="#mwt754" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-reuters210518_311-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"reuters210518"}}'><a href="#cite_note-reuters210518-311" id="mwCH0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCH4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCH8">[</span>310<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCIA">]</span></span></a></sup> In August 2020, BP promised to increase its annual low carbon investments to $5<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwCIE"> </span>billion by 2030.<sup about="#mwt755" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-cnn040820_293-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"cnn040820"}}'><a href="#cite_note-cnn040820-293" id="mwCII"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCIM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCIQ">[</span>292<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCIU">]</span></span></a></sup> The company announced plans to transform into an integrated energy company, with a renewed focus on investing away from oil and into low-carbon technologies.<sup about="#mwt758" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-312" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-312"}}'><a href="#cite_note-312" id="mwCIY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCIc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCIg">[</span>311<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCIk">]</span></span></a></sup> It has set targets to have a renewables portfolio of 20<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwCIo"> </span>GW by 2025, and 50<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwCIs"> </span>GW by 2030.<sup about="#mwt761" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-313" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-313"}}'><a href="#cite_note-313" id="mwCIw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCI0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCI4">[</span>312<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCI8">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwCJA">BP operates nine wind farms in seven states of the U.S., and held an interest in another in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hawaii" title="Hawaii" id="mwCJE">Hawaii</a> with a net generating capacity of 1,679<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwCJI"> </span>MW.<sup about="#mwt762" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-BP-wind_243-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"BP-wind"}}'><a href="#cite_note-BP-wind-243" id="mwCJM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCJQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCJU">[</span>242<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCJY">]</span></span></a></sup> It is also in process to acquire 50% non-operating stake in the Empire Wind off New York and Beacon Wind off Massachusetts offshore wind farms.<sup about="#mwt763" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-reuters100920_167-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"reuters100920"}}'><a href="#cite_note-reuters100920-167" id="mwCJc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCJg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCJk">[</span>166<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCJo">]</span></span></a></sup> BP and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tesla,_Inc." title="Tesla, Inc." id="mwCJs">Tesla, Inc.</a> are cooperating for testing the energy storage by battery at the Titan 1 wind farm.<sup about="#mwt764" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-AR18-wind_314-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"AR18-wind"}}'><a href="#cite_note-AR18-wind-314" id="mwCJw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCJ0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCJ4">[</span>313<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCJ8">]</span></span></a></sup> BP Launchpad has also invested in ONYX InSight, one of the leading providers of predictive analytic solutions serving the wind industry.<sup about="#mwt765" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-energyvoice230120_315-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"energyvoice230120"}}'><a href="#cite_note-energyvoice230120-315" id="mwCKA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCKE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCKI">[</span>314<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCKM">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwCKQ">In Brazil, BP owns two ethanol producers—<i id="mwCKU">Companhia Nacional de Açúcar e Álcool</i> and<i id="mwCKY">Tropical BioEnergia</i>—with three ethanol mills.<sup about="#mwt767" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-reuters140911_285-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"reuters140911"}}'><a href="#cite_note-reuters140911-285" id="mwCKc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCKg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCKk">[</span>284<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCKo">]</span></span></a></sup> These mills produce around <span about="#mwt766" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCKs" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"convert","href":"./Template:Convert"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"800000"},"2":{"wt":"m3/a"},"3":{"wt":"oilbbl/a"}},"i":0}}]}'>800,000 cubic metres per annum (5,000,000</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt766"> </span><span about="#mwt766">bbl/a)</span> of ethanol equivalent.<sup about="#mwt768" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-spw201217_316-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"spw201217"}}'><a href="#cite_note-spw201217-316" id="mwCKw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCK0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCK4">[</span>315<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCK8">]</span></span></a></sup> BP has invested in an agricultural biotechnology company Chromatin, a company developing crops that can grow on marginal land and that are optimized to be used as feedstock for biofuel.<sup about="#mwt769" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Herndon2011_317-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Herndon2011"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Herndon2011-317" id="mwCLA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCLE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCLI">[</span>316<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCLM">]</span></span></a></sup> Its joint venture with DuPont called Butamax, which has developed the patented bio-butanol-producing technology,<sup about="#mwt770" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-delaware280815_318-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"delaware280815"}}'><a href="#cite_note-delaware280815-318" id="mwCLQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCLU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCLY">[</span>317<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCLc">]</span></span></a></sup> and owns an isobutanol plant in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scandia,_Kansas" title="Scandia, Kansas" id="mwCLg">Scandia, Kansas</a>, United States.<sup about="#mwt771" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-biomass030417_152-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"biomass030417"}}'><a href="#cite_note-biomass030417-152" id="mwCLk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCLo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCLs">[</span>151<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCLw">]</span></span></a></sup> In addition BP owns biomethane production facilities in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canton,_Michigan" title="Canton, Michigan" id="mwCL0">Canton, Michigan</a>, and North Shelby, Tennessee, as well as share of facilities under construction in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oklahoma_City" title="Oklahoma City" id="mwCL4">Oklahoma City</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Atlanta" title="Atlanta" id="mwCL8">Atlanta</a>.<sup about="#mwt772" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Hardcastle17_151-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Hardcastle17"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Hardcastle17-151" id="mwCMA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCME"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCMI">[</span>150<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCMM">]</span></span></a></sup> BP's subsidiary Air BP supplies aviation biofuel at <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oslo_Airport,_Gardermoen" title="Oslo Airport, Gardermoen" id="mwCMQ">Oslo</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Halmstad_Airport" title="Halmstad Airport" id="mwCMU">Halmstad</a>, and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bergen_Airport,_Flesland" title="Bergen Airport, Flesland" id="mwCMY">Bergen</a> airports.<sup about="#mwt773" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-aviationpross210817_319-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"aviationpross210817"}}'><a href="#cite_note-aviationpross210817-319" id="mwCMc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCMg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCMk">[</span>318<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCMo">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwCMs">BP owns a 43% stake in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lightsource_BP" title="Lightsource BP" id="mwCMw">Lightsource BP</a>, a company which focuses on the managing and maintaining <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Photovoltaic_power_station" title="Photovoltaic power station" id="mwCM0">solar farms</a>. <span about="#mwt774" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCM4" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"As of","href":"./Template:As_of"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"2017"}},"i":0}}]}'>As of 2017</span><sup class="plainlinks noexcerpt noprint asof-tag update" style="display:none;" about="#mwt774"><a rel="mw:ExtLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=BP&amp;action=edit" class="external text" data-mw-original-href="//en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=BP&amp;action=edit"><span typeof="mw:Entity">[</span>update<span typeof="mw:Entity">]</span></a></sup><span typeof="mw:Nowiki" about="#mwt774"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_potentially_dated_statements_from_2017" about="#mwt774"/><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:All_articles_containing_potentially_dated_statements" about="#mwt774" id="mwCM8"/>, Lightsource has commissioned 1.3<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwCNA"> </span>GW of solar capacity and manages about 2<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwCNE"> </span>GW of solar capacity. It plans to increase the capacity up to 8<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwCNI"> </span>GW through projects in the United States, India, Europe and the Middle East.<sup about="#mwt775" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-bloomberg151217_149-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"bloomberg151217"}}'><a href="#cite_note-bloomberg151217-149" id="mwCNM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCNQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCNU">[</span>148<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCNY">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt776" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-reuters151217_150-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"reuters151217"}}'><a href="#cite_note-reuters151217-150" id="mwCNc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCNg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCNk">[</span>149<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCNo">]</span></span></a></sup> BP has invested $20<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwCNs"> </span>million in Israeli quick-charging battery firm StoreDot Ltd.<sup about="#mwt777" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-bloomberg240518_320-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"bloomberg240518"}}'><a href="#cite_note-bloomberg240518-320" id="mwCNw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCN0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCN4">[</span>319<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCN8">]</span></span></a></sup> It operates electric vehicle charging networks in the UK under its subsidiary <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/BP_Chargemaster" title="BP Chargemaster" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCOA">BP Chargemaster</a>, and in China via a joint venture with <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Didi_Chuxing" title="Didi Chuxing" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCOE">Didi Chuxing</a>.<sup about="#mwt778" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-icis141020_157-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"icis141020"}}'><a href="#cite_note-icis141020-157" id="mwCOI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCOM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCOQ">[</span>156<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCOU">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwCOY">In partnership with <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ørsted_(company)" title="Ørsted (company)" id="mwCOc">Ørsted A/S</a>, BP plans a 50<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwCOg"> </span>MV <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electrolyser" title="Electrolyser" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCOk">electrolyser</a> at the Lingen refinery to produce hydrogen using North Sea wind power. Production is expected to begin in 2024.<sup about="#mwt779" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ft101120_321-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ft101120"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ft101120-321" id="mwCOo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCOs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCOw">[</span>320<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCO0">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwCO4">BP is a majority shareholder in carbon offset developer Finite Carbon,<sup about="#mwt780" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-reuters161220_168-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"reuters161220"}}'><a href="#cite_note-reuters161220-168" id="mwCO8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCPA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCPE">[</span>167<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCPI">]</span></span></a></sup> and acquired 9<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwCPM"> </span>GW of US solar projects in 2021.<sup about="#mwt783" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-322" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-322"}}'><a href="#cite_note-322" id="mwCPQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCPU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCPY">[</span>321<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCPc">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwCPg">In 2023, following the announcement of record profits, the company scaled back their emissions targets. Originally, the company promised a 35-40% cut of emissions by the end of the decade. On 7 February, BP revised the target to a 20-30% cut in emissions, stating that it needed to keep up with the current demands for oil and gas.<sup about="#mwt786" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-323" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-323"}}'><a href="#cite_note-323" id="mwCPk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCPo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCPs">[</span>322<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCPw">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

